From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:13:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Fix the RAG review findings: list code blocks, URL
 credentials, MCP output cleaning

- Crawled pages: code blocks and tables inside list items (install steps) were
  squashed into one inline line; such items now become separate blocks, so the
  chunker keeps the code whole with its line breaks and indentation.
- qdrant_url: credentials in the URL are refused (they would sit in the plain
  config file and in connection errors); an invalid port is a clear error and
  get_status() no longer raises ValueError for it.
- search_knowledge (MCP): source and content go through sanitize_untrusted, so
  invisible carriers (Unicode tags, zero-width, bidi controls) in crawled pages
  or community packs never reach the client's model.
- Code ingest uses POSIX relative paths in the source, so point ids are the same
  on Windows and Linux.
- Crawl failure log goes through redact_secrets.
- .gitignore: models/embeddings (the FastEmbed cache under the default
  models_dir in a source checkout).
- Tests for the above plus claimed but untested behaviour: NaN vectors are
  refused, loopback servers work without a key, snapshot pruning keeps the newest
  five, a storage lock held by another process gives the documented message.

